---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  role="visitor"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: "Home", href: "/" },
    { label: "Methods & quality" },
    { label: "How the models work" },
  ]}
  backHref="/methods/evaluation-framework"
>
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-4xl prose prose-gray">
    <h1>How the Models Work</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Impact analysis model — ridge regression</h2>
      <p>
        The impact analysis tool estimates the contribution of each mobility measure to observed
        KPI changes across Living Labs. It uses <strong>ridge regression</strong>, a variant of
        linear regression designed to handle situations where the number of predictors (measures)
        is large relative to the number of observations (cities).
      </p>

      <h3>What it does</h3>
      <p>
        Ridge regression fits a model that relates each measure's presence (binary: implemented
        or not) to the observed change in a KPI value. The regularisation parameter (lambda)
        prevents any single measure from dominating the model when data coverage is limited.
      </p>

      <h3>Inputs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Before/after KPI values per city</li>
        <li>Binary indicator of which measures each city implemented</li>
        <li>City-level covariates (where available)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Outputs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Estimated coefficient for each measure — its associated direction of KPI change</li>
        <li>Evidence strength badge based on data coverage (Limited / Moderate / Strong)</li>
        <li>Ranking of measures by estimated impact magnitude</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Important assumptions</h3>
      <p>
        The model assumes linear relationships between measures and KPI changes. It cannot
        establish causal relationships — only statistical associations. Results should be
        interpreted in conjunction with local context. See
        <a href="/methods/limitations" class="text-primary hover:underline">Limitations</a> for details.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/tools/impact_analysis" class="text-primary hover:underline">Use the impact analysis tool →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>MCDA model — PROMETHEE II</h2>
      <p>
        The multi-criteria decision analysis (MCDA) tool uses the
        <strong>PROMETHEE II</strong> (Preference Ranking Organisation METHod for Enrichment
        Evaluations) method to rank business activities for New Shared Mobility according to
        multiple criteria simultaneously.
      </p>

      <h3>What it does</h3>
      <p>
        PROMETHEE II computes pairwise preference comparisons between alternatives (NSM business
        activities) across multiple weighted goals. For each pair, it calculates how much one
        alternative is preferred over another. Aggregating these pairwise comparisons yields
        a net flow score (phi) for each alternative, and the alternatives are ranked by descending
        phi value.
      </p>

      <h3>Inputs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Set of alternatives (NSM business activities)</li>
        <li>Goal weights per stakeholder perspective</li>
        <li>Performance scores per alternative per goal</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Outputs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Net flow (phi) score per alternative — higher is better</li>
        <li>Ranked list of alternatives by perspective</li>
        <li>GAIA plane visualisation showing trade-offs and stakeholder alignment</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>GAIA companion</h3>
      <p>
        The GAIA (Geometrical Analysis for Interactive Aid) plane is a 2D projection of the
        PROMETHEE results that helps visualise conflicts and synergies between goals and
        alternatives. The decision axis (d-axis) indicates the overall PROMETHEE ranking direction.
      </p>

      <h3>Important assumptions</h3>
      <p>
        Goal weights reflect stakeholder priorities from expert surveys and may not reflect all
        real-world contexts. Performance scores are derived from platform data. See
        <a href="/methods/limitations" class="text-primary hover:underline">Limitations</a> for details.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/tools/mcda_analysis/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Use the decision tool →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="not-prose mt-8 flex gap-4 text-sm">
      <a href="/methods/limitations" class="text-primary hover:underline">Next: Limitations →</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</Layout>
